LICENSE_SRC.MAP -- the license text found in each file under src/
==============================================================

Generated by scripts/license-map.py; do not edit. It reports which header a file
carries, not which terms apply: for that, LICENSE and LICENSE_CODE.

    class  files  header in the file
    -----  -----  --------------------------------------------------------
    B       1382  Sun's "Copyright Header" (the BSD+ grant)
    BC         7  that header, and after it a CDDL header
    S         11  a Sun copyright line only, no grant text
    N          9  no copyright or license text
    X          7  binary
    total   1416

Among the 1389 files with that header (B and BC) there is 1 distinct text, the year
and the file name aside.

Every file that is not class B, which is where a question about terms comes from.
The "needed" column is measured for classes S and N only: which path stops when the
file is missing; "-" means not measured. Method: all 20 files were removed from a copy,
the files the build stopped for put back, then the reduced and the full set built into
the same OUTDIR with the same SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH. All six outputs (openboot.bin, q.bin,
reset.bin, 1up-md.bin, 1up-hv.bin, nvram1) were byte-identical (md5 on the Solaris side).
Needed on the gnu path: 4; on the sun path (legion, Solaris 10,
Sun Studio 11): 7 -- the four, and aschk/aslex.l, vdev_snet.s, obp/firmware.rel.
One sun-path run stopped at mmu_common.o with no message in the log; the same command
passed on the next run. Not explained.

